2026-10-20T21:06:14.0572674Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.0573224Z -               '    # BAD: user has full control of URL\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.0574353Z -               '    resp = requests.get("https://" + target + ".example.com/data/")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.0575102Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.0575729Z -               '    # GOOD: `subdomain` is controlled by the server.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.0576557Z -               '    subdomain = "europe" if target == "EU" else "world"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.0577444Z -               '    resp = requests.get("https://" + subdomain + ".example.com/data/")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.0578101Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.0578432Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.0580759Z +               'To guard against XXE attacks with the `lxml` library, you should create a parser with `resolve_entities` set to `false`. This means that no entity expansion is undertaken, although standard predefined entities such as `&gt;`, for writing `>` inside the text of an XML element, are still allowed.\n' +
