2026-10-20T21:06:14.1184569Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1185396Z +             text: 'Writing user input directly to a web page allows for a cross-site scripting vulnerability.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1186008Z +           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1186413Z +           help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1186972Z +             markdown: '# Reflected server-side cross-site scripting\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1188375Z +               'Directly writing user input (for example, an HTTP request parameter) to a webpage without properly sanitizing the input first, allows for a cross-site scripting vulnerability.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1189467Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1189794Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1190270Z +               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1192192Z +               'To guard against cross-site scripting, consider escaping the input before writing user input to the page. The standard library provides escaping functions: `html.escape()` for Python 3.2 upwards or `cgi.escape()` older versions of Python. Most frameworks also provide their own escaping functions, for example `flask.escape()`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1193647Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1194328Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1194701Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1196767Z +               'The following example is a minimal flask app which shows a safe and unsafe way to render the given name back to the page. The first view is unsafe as `first_name` is not escaped, leaving the page vulnerable to cross-site scripting attacks. The second view is safe as `first_name` is escaped, so it is not vulnerable to cross-site scripting attacks.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1198272Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1198581Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1199036Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1199600Z +               'from flask import Flask, request, make_response, escape\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1200202Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1200591Z +               'app = Flask(__name__)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1200959Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1201444Z +               "@app.route('/unsafe')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1201903Z +               'def unsafe():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1202459Z +               "    first_name = request.args.get('name', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1203128Z +               '    return make_response("Your name is " + first_name)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1203578Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1204295Z +               "@app.route('/safe')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1204759Z +               'def safe():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1205327Z +               "    first_name = request.args.get('name', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1206025Z +               '    return make_response("Your name is " + escape(first_name))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1206504Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1206931Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1207304Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1207727Z +               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1209010Z +               '* OWASP: [XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1210275Z +               '* Wikipedia: [Cross-site scripting](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross-site_scripting).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1211438Z +               '* Python Library Reference: [html.escape()](https://docs.python.org/3/library/html.html#html.escape).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1212432Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-79](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1213440Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-116](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/116.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1214516Z +             text: '# Reflected server-side cross-site scripting\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1215725Z +               'Directly writing user input (for example, an HTTP request parameter) to a webpage without properly sanitizing the input first, allows for a cross-site scripting vulnerability.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1216809Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1218079Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1218525Z +               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1220440Z +               'To guard against cross-site scripting, consider escaping the input before writing user input to the page. The standard library provides escaping functions: `html.escape()` for Python 3.2 upwards or `cgi.escape()` older versions of Python. Most frameworks also provide their own escaping functions, for example `flask.escape()`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1222058Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1222533Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1222895Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1225153Z +               'The following example is a minimal flask app which shows a safe and unsafe way to render the given name back to the page. The first view is unsafe as `first_name` is not escaped, leaving the page vulnerable to cross-site scripting attacks. The second view is safe as `first_name` is escaped, so it is not vulnerable to cross-site scripting attacks.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1226681Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1226996Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1227495Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1228039Z +               'from flask import Flask, request, make_response, escape\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1228640Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1229027Z +               'app = Flask(__name__)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1229402Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1229916Z +               "@app.route('/unsafe')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1230342Z +               'def unsafe():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1230944Z +               "    first_name = request.args.get('name', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1231553Z +               '    return make_response("Your name is " + first_name)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1232036Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1232516Z +               "@app.route('/safe')\n" +
