2026-10-20T21:06:14.1318347Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1318789Z +             text: 'Writing user input directly to an HTTP header makes code vulnerable to attack by header splitting.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1319402Z -             text: 'Interpreting unsanitized user input as code allows a malicious user to perform arbitrary code execution.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1319484Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1319583Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1319771Z +             markdown: '# HTTP Response Splitting\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1320402Z +               'Directly writing user input (for example, an HTTP request parameter) to an HTTP header can lead to an HTTP response-splitting vulnerability.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1320568Z -             markdown: '# Code injection\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1321859Z -               'Directly evaluating user input (for example, an HTTP request parameter) as code without properly sanitizing the input first allows an attacker arbitrary code execution. This can occur when user input is passed to code that interprets it as an expression to be evaluated, such as `eval` or `exec`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1321955Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1322914Z +               'If user-controlled input is used in an HTTP header that allows line break characters, an attacker can inject additional headers or control the response body, leading to vulnerabilities such as XSS or cache poisoning.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1322999Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1323099Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1323226Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1323634Z +               'Ensure that user input containing line break characters is not written to an HTTP header.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1325058Z -               'Avoid including user input in any expression that may be dynamically evaluated. If user input must be included, use context-specific escaping before including it. It is important that the correct escaping is used for the type of evaluation that will occur.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1325156Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1325243Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1325364Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1326088Z +               'In the following example, the case marked BAD writes user input to the header name. In the GOOD case, input is first escaped to not contain any line break characters.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1327914Z -               'The following example shows two functions setting a name from a request. The first function uses `exec` to execute the `setname` function. This is dangerous as it can allow a malicious user to execute arbitrary code on the server. For example, the user could supply the value `"\' + subprocess.call(\'rm -rf\') + \'"` to destroy the server\'s file system. The second function calls the `setname` function directly and is thus safe.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1328152Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1328247Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1328357Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1328540Z +               '@app.route("/example_bad")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1328687Z +               'def example_bad():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1328896Z +               '    rfs_header = request.args["rfs_header"]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1329055Z +               '    response = Response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1329270Z +               '    custom_header = "X-MyHeader-" + rfs_header\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1329521Z +               '    # BAD: User input is used as part of the header name.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1329761Z +               '    response.headers[custom_header] = "HeaderValue" \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1329907Z +               '    return response\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1329988Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1330157Z +               '@app.route("/example_good")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1330300Z +               'def example_bad():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1330509Z +               '    rfs_header = request.args["rfs_header"]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1330669Z +               '    response = Response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1331223Z +               '    custom_header = "X-MyHeader-" + rfs_header.replace("\\n", "").replace("\\r","").replace(":","")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1331498Z +               '    # GOOD: Line break characters are removed from the input.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1331738Z +               '    response.headers[custom_header] = "HeaderValue" \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1331877Z +               '    return response\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1332021Z -               'urlpatterns = [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1332191Z -               '    # Route to code_execution\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1332562Z -               "    url(r'^code-ex1$', code_execution_bad, name='code-execution-bad'),\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1332879Z -               "    url(r'^code-ex2$', code_execution_good, name='code-execution-good')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1332981Z -               ']\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1333071Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1333242Z -               'def code_execution(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1333420Z -               "    if request.method == 'POST':\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1333759Z -               "        first_name = base64.decodestring(request.POST.get('first_name', ''))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1334246Z -               '        #BAD -- Allow user to define code to be run.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1334446Z -               `        exec("setname('%s')" % first_name)\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1334547Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1334719Z -               'def code_execution(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1334892Z -               "    if request.method == 'POST':\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1335223Z -               "        first_name = base64.decodestring(request.POST.get('first_name', ''))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1335411Z -               '        #GOOD --Call code directly\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1335572Z -               '        setname(first_name)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1335670Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1335766Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1335851Z                 '\n' +
